{"name":"Sunshade","hex":"#fa9d49","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"sunshade","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Something to keep the sun off, or create shade from the sun; a parasol or awning."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sunshade"}],"entries":[{"title":"Brise soleil","blocks":[{"text":"Brise soleil, sometimes brise-soleil, is an architectural feature of a building that reduces its heat gain by deflecting incoming sunlight. The system allows low-level sunlight to enter a building in the mornings, evenings and during winter but cuts out direct light during summer."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dd/Two_Point_Seven_Facades_Charles_Wells_Brewery_Brise_Soleil.jpg/330px-Two_Point_Seven_Facades_Charles_Wells_Brewery_Brise_Soleil.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brise_soleil"},{"title":"Shade (shadow)","blocks":[{"text":"Shade is the blocking of sunlight by any object, and also the shadow created by that object. It may refer to blocking of sunlight by a roof, a tree, an umbrella, a window shade or blind, wall, curtains, or other objects."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cc/Tree_shadows_on_moss_%28Unsplash%29.jpg/330px-Tree_shadows_on_moss_%28Unsplash%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shade_(shadow)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/95/Millennium_Point_Exterior.jpg/250px-Millennium_Point_Exterior.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/95/Millennium_Point_Exterior.jpg/500px-Millennium_Point_Exterior.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/95/Millennium_Point_Exterior.